{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to build the Cinescope cinema seat-booking web app described in `spec/README.md`, as the Angular application in the Nx project `cinescope` (`apps/cinescope`), following the tickets in `spec/tickets/01-…07-…` in order. Instructions: do not ask questions; where the spec is silent, choose the simplest option that satisfies it; finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. Rules from the spec: use pnpm only (no npm/yarn); the app runs on `http://localhost:4200` (do not change the port); do not add dependencies; do not edit `db.json` by hand; the app is desktop-only (1280×720+); all UI text in English; do not change the date logic to show screenings; use UI library components (Angular Material) for buttons, text fields, checkbox, toast and datepicker; seat map, legend and selected-seats panel are drawn by the app.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Angular 22 standalone components, zoneless, signals (`signal`, `computed`), `toSignal`/`takeUntilDestroyed` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop`, OnPush change detection, control-flow blocks (`@if/@for/@switch`), strict templates.\n   - Angular Router: routes with `component`, `children: []` placeholders, `canActivate` functional guards returning `UrlTree` redirects, `queryParamMap`, `paramMap`, `router.navigateByUrl` / `navigate`.\n   - HttpClient with `provideHttpClient(withFetch())`; backend json-server 0.17.4 at `http://localhost:3000` (`pnpm api`).\n   - Angular Material 22: `MatButtonModule`, `MatDatepickerModule` (with `provideNativeDateAdapter`), `MatInputModule`/`MatFormFieldModule`, `MatCheckboxModule`, `MatSnackBar` (`openFromComponent`, `MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA`).\n   - Booking persisted in `sessionStorage` under key `cinescope.booking`.\n   - Vitest unit tests via `@angular/build:unit-test` (`pnpm nx test cinescope`), ESLint via `pnpm nx lint cinescope`, Prettier (`.prettierrc`: singleQuote, printWidth 100).\n   - Seat geometry: 15 rows, 24 columns, aisles between columns 4/5 and 20/21, entrance gap in rows 1–10 (left block empty), accessible seats R1C10–R1C15, couches in row 15 (1-2 … 23-24), seat price tiers (rows 1–5 25.00, 6–10 32.00, 11–14 39.00, couch 89.00 PLN).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `spec/README.md`, `spec/stack.md`, `spec/tickets/*.md` — read only. Tickets are unchecked (`- [ ]`) and not yet ticked.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts` — modified: providers are `provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners()`, `provideRouter(appRoutes)`, `provideHttpClient(withFetch())`, `provideNativeDateAdapter()`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts` — current content:\n     ```ts\n     export const appRoutes: Route[] = [\n       { path: '', component: MovieList },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/seats', component: SeatMap },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/summary', component: Summary, canActivate: [unpaidBookingGuard] },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/checkout', component: Checkout, canActivate: [unpaidBookingGuard] },\n       { path: 'confirmation', component: Confirmation, canActivate: [paidBookingGuard] },\n       { path: '**', redirectTo: '' },\n     ];\n     ```\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/models.ts` — created: `Movie`, `Screening`, `Reservation`, `NewReservation = Omit<Reservation,'id'>`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/cinema.api.ts` — created: `CinemaApi` (`movies()`, `movie(id)`, `screenings()`, `screening(id)`, `createReservation(r)`), BASE_URL `http://localhost:3000`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/dates.ts` — created: `startOfToday`, `toIsoDate`, `parseIsoDate` (regex + round-trip check, returns null when invalid), `addDays`, `weekdayName`, `showDate(isoDate, time)` → e.g. `Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/movie-list.ts|.html|.scss` — created. Loads `forkJoin({movies, screenings})` in constructor; `state` signal `'loading'|'error'|'loaded'`; `selectedDate` from query param (invalid or before today → today); `dayOptions` (5 days, labels `Today` then weekday names); `pickerDate` is non-null only when the selected day is not one of the five; `cards` computed (movies with screenings on the selected day, screenings sorted by time); `selectDate(date)` navigates to `/?date=YYYY-MM-DD`. Template has data-testids day-picker, day-button (data-date, data-selected), date-picker (on the input), movies-loading, movies-error, movies-retry-button, movies-empty, movie-list, movie-card (data-movie-id), movie-title, movie-genre, movie-runtime (`{{n}} min`), movie-format, screening-button (data-screening-id, routerLink to `/screenings/:id/seats`).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-map/auditorium.ts` — created: `buildAuditorium()` returns `RowLayout[]` with `blocks: [left, middle, right]`; items are `SeatItem {kind:'seat', row, column, id, accessible}` or `CouchItem {kind:'couch', row, start, end, ids}`; `seatId`, `isAccessible`. Verified via node script: 308 elements, 296 seats, 12 couches, 6 accessible.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-map/seat-map.ts|.html|.scss` — created/modified. Loads screening then movie by `paramMap` (any failure → `navigateByUrl('/')`), then `booking.start(screening.id)`. `stateOf(item)` → 'unavailable' (occupied; couch if either id occupied) > 'selected' > 'accessible' > 'available'. `STATE_COLOURS` = #2E7D32 / #F9A825 / #C62828 / #1565C0. `select(item)` ignores unavailable; calls `booking.toggle(screening.id, ids)`; on `'limit'` shows toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`. `cancel()` clears booking and goes to `/`. `continueToSummary()` no-ops when nothing selected. Template: title `Choose your seats`, subtitle `Show Date: …`, seat-limit-info, screen-indicator `SCREEN`, seat-map with seat-row/row-label-left/right/aisle/seat/couch, legend (legend-item data-state), selected-seats panel (selected-seats-count, selected-seats-row data-row), cancel-button, continue-button (disabled when empty). Block widths: seat 30px, gap 4px, aisle 64px, end blocks 132px, middle 540px.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/booking/tickets.ts` — created: `COUCH_ROW=15`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`, `seatId`, `parseSeatId`, `seatPrice(row)`, `formatPrice(n)` → `\"25.00 PLN\"`, `ticketsFor(ids)` → sorted `Ticket {row,isCouch,ids,seatLabel,columnsLabel,price}` with row-15 pairing (odd column with +1). seatLabel is `12` or `Couch 3-4`; columnsLabel is `12` or `3-4`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/booking/booking.store.ts` — created: `BookingStore` (providedIn root). `Booking {screeningId, seats: string[], form: CheckoutValues, paidEmail: string|null}`; `MAX_SEATS=10`; methods: `booking` (readonly signal), `seatCount`, `selectedFor(screeningId)`, `start(screeningId)` (keeps an existing unpaid booking for the same screening, otherwise creates an empty one), `toggle(screeningId, ids)` → `'added'|'removed'|'limit'|'ignored'`, `removeTickets(ids)`, `setForm(partial)`, `markPaid(email)`, `clear()`. Persists to sessionStorage on every write.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/booking/booking.guards.ts` — created: `unpaidBookingGuard` (booking exists, unpaid, screeningId equals route id, seats > 0, else `/`), `paidBookingGuard` (`booking?.paidEmail != null`, else `/`).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/toast/toast.ts` — created: `ToastMessage` component (`<span data-testid=\"toast\">`), `Toast.show(message)` → MatSnackBar with duration 4000.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/summary/summary.ts|.html|.scss` — created. Loads screening and movie (failure → `/`). Items: summary-item, summary-item-title, -datetime (`{{date}} {{time}}`), -row, -seat (seatLabel), -price, -remove-button (`remove(ticket.ids)`; if no seats left → seats route). Total `Total: {{formatPrice(total())}}` (summary-total). Buttons back-button (→ seats), confirm-button (→ checkout). Title `Your tickets`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/checkout/checkout.validation.ts` — created: `validateCheckout(values)` implements the spec's messages and rules (required messages `X is required`; first/last ≥ 2 chars; email regex `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`; confirm equals email; phone empty or `/^\\d{9}$/`; terms must be true).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/checkout/checkout.ts|.html|.scss` — created. Values come from `booking.booking()?.form`; inputs are `type=\"text\"` (not email, to avoid sanitisation); `patch(field, value)` writes to the store; `touch(field)` on blur (touched state is local, not persisted); terms `setTerms(checked)` marks touched; `shownError(field)` shows the message only if touched; `pay()` marks all touched, shows toast `The form contains errors` when invalid, otherwise `submitting=true`, calls `api.createReservation({screeningId, seats (ticket ids in summary order), customer{firstName,lastName,email,phone}, totalPrice})`; on success `markPaid(email)` and navigate to `/confirmation`; on error toast `Payment failed. Please try again.` and re-enable. Pay button label `Pay {{formatPrice(total())}}` or `Processing…` while submitting. Back → summary. Data-testids: checkout-title, first-name-input, last-name-input, email-input, confirm-email-input, phone-input, terms-checkbox, first-name-label etc., -error ids, checkout-back-button, pay-button.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/confirmation/confirmation.ts|.html|.scss` — created. Heading `Payment successful` (confirmation-heading), message `Your tickets will be sent shortly to {{email()}}` (confirmation-message), `Continue` (confirmation-continue-button) calls `booking.clear()` and navigates to `/`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/logic.spec.ts` — created: Vitest tests for auditorium counts, ticket pricing and couch grouping, checkout validation rules, email/phone patterns, date parsing and show date formatting. All 9 tests pass.\n   - `spec/tickets/*.md` — NOT yet modified; all boxes still `- [ ]`.\n   - `.pnpm-store/` — un